            "tender": {
                "id": "ocds-h6vhtk-06d971",
                "legalBasis": {
                    "id": "2023/54",
                    "scheme": "UKPGA",
                    "uri": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2023/54/contents"
                },
                "title": "Recreation Ground Refresh",
                "description": "Summary: \nUpgrade of facilities on the Layer de la Haye recreation ground, replacing/upgrading some of the existing equipment as well as extending the type of equipment available.  The chosen supplier will be able to supply and install all equipment to appropriate safety standards, as well as ensuring safety during works, removal of all spoils/waste and the provision of safety inspections.  Install within 6 months of contract award is desired, although it is recognised that weather my impact this timeline.  Hence the estimated contract duration is suggested as 12 months to cover all eventualities.\nDetail:\nWe want to engage a single supplier for the entire solution install - Recreation Ground Refresh on New Cut, Layer de la Haye, opposite the Village Hall.\nOut of the existing items, we want to keep the following:\n•\tNest swing\n•\tSpace net\nWe want to remove:\n•\tExisting 2 pairs of swings\n•\tExisting child trim trail\nAnything not mentioned in the keep/remove sections above, we are open to your suggestions (e.g. the existing slide could stay or be removed if replaced by something more modern).\nWe want the following:\n•\tA design proposal that considers best flow and suitable separation between age related elements (don't be constrained by the current layout)\n•\tBasketball/football nets (for the existing basketball courts) - no solid panels and rectangular in shape.  Renew surface.  Consider location - where it is, or should we move it (e.g. to accommodate siting of a zip wire)?\n•\t10 to 12 separate pieces of teen to adult gym equipment (i.e. not built as one unit) \n•\tAccessible carousel for all capabilities (wheelchair/able bodied)\n•\tAccessible trampoline (wheelchair and able bodied alike)\n•\t4-seater see saw (with tyres as bump stops)\n•\tInclusive sensory panels/boards to engage a variety of ages in creative play and/or communication\n•\tTrim trail including stepper platforms, crawl net, spiders web climber, curved traverse net\n•\tSwings - 5 in total - 2 normal, 2 baby 1 inclusive (if can be used by abled child too)\n•\t4 tower junior multi-play \n•\tPreschool junior play ship \n•\tTeen pod with normal seating, wind break side covering and no table\n•\tColoured wet pour where appropriate (quote for just under kit or an entire area), advise what is best for maintenance\n•\tGrass matting where needed\n•\tFor gym - all in a line or square, what is the best surface?\n•\tZip wire - but where? (placement to take into account any potential resident concerns...)\nAll quotes must include:\n•\tSignage for all kit as appropriate plus additional CCTV/general warning signs (enough to cover whole recreation area so will depend on design)\n•\tRecommended annual plan for routine maintenance and independent inspection regime\n•\tInsurance cover for product left on site before install and secure storage (i.e. supplier retains responsibility in the case of vandalism/theft until fully installed)\n•\tRemoval of all spoils\n•\tDelivery/Install and Harris Fencing or other security measures\n•\tWelfare provision\n•\tLength of warranty period\n•\tLead time to deliver and install",
                "status": "active",
                "items": [
                    {
                        "id": "1",
                        "additionalClassifications": [
                            {
                                "scheme": "CPV",
                                "id": "37535200",
                                "description": "Playground equipment"
                            }
                        ],
                        "deliveryAddresses": [
