                "title": "Window Cleaning Services",
                "description": "PROCUREMENT DESCRIPTION\nTo carry out window cleaning on all glazing and specified building areas at the Royal Armouries Museum and New Dock Hall in Leeds. Complying with all Health & Safety regulations (inc. Working at Height) and following industrial best practices.\nCURRENT SERVICE SCOPE\nFortnightly Visits\n•   Ground floor building entrance areas including auto doors (inside and outside including the fold back glass inner doors)\n•   Dockside Ground floor frontage including the RA shop and Masters Restaurant Windows (Inside and outside)\n•   New Dock Hall: All of frontage glazing inside and outside\nQuarterly Visits – Jan – Apr – Jul – Oct\n•   Regular windows and glazing – both internal and external surfaces \n•   Slit windows – both internal and external surfaces \n•   Triangular viewing windows – both internal and external surfaces \n•   Regular recessed windows – both internal and external surfaces\n•   Juliette windows (can be fully opened) – both internal and external surfaces \n•   Internal Doors/windows to street from shop and restaurant\n•   Office skylights 5th Floor – both internal and external surfaces \n•   Internal balconies, glazed bridges, window internal balconies and stairwell glazing - both sides \n•   Facia of ‘Street’ – both internal and external surfaces\n•   Hall of Steel’ internal and external surfaces and both sides of all stairway glazing\n•   To include internal glazing of all four galleries\nAnnual and 6 monthly Tasks (Apr/Oct)\n•   Panoramic glass lifts – by appointment and under the direct control of our lift maintenance service provider (internally). (Yearly task) \n•   External canopy over the Tiltyard (Annually- April)\n•   Hall of Steel ground and 1st floor building frontage, including brickwork (6 Monthly Apr/Oct)\n•   Street’ skylights - external surfaces (6 Monthly Apr/Oct)\n•   Craft Court Windows (1st Floor, smoking, shelter canopy, Cycle Storage (6 Monthly April/Oct)\n•   External balcony of ‘Pearl’ Suite’ Both sides\nESTIMATED CONTRACT VALUE (INCL. VAT): £400,000\n•   Initial term: £240,000\n•   Optional extensions: £160,000",
